# Raspberry Pi Powered Bird Audio Detector

A Raspberry Pi-based environmental audio monitoring system that uses machine learning to identify local bird species through their vocalizations.

## Overview 

This project uses a Raspberry Pi Zero 2 W and an external microphone to continuously record environmental audio, identify bird vocalizations using machine learning, and collect detection data for long-term observation.

The system was designed to monitor local bird activity and explore patterns in species presence and vocalization over time, along with its correlation with temperature and sunrise/sunset. 

The file raspberry.py contains the code for the Raspberry Pi; actual detections are processed in the actual website. View detections at birdingwith.me/data. 


